QuestGuidance.Register("en",388,{
[12385]="700215AD\n1\tThe second half of the broken amulet may be found on shades throughout the Lich Bluffs. When you locate the other half of the broken amulet, seek out and locate the hermit Lhudd in a small grove of trees to the west of the road called the Hall of Sanctuary.\t\n2\tCollect the second half of the broken amulet\tThe second half of the broken amulet may be found on shades throughout the Lich Bluffs. When you locate the other half of the broken amulet, seek out and locate the hermit Lhudd in a small grove of trees to the west of the road called the Hall of Sanctuary.\n3\tBring the two halves of the amulet to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary\tLhudd the hermit dwells at the Hall of Sanctuary, west of the main road and south-west of Mincham's camp. Mincham told you to bring both halves of the amulet to Lhudd the hermit.\n",
[12386]="7006BB25\n1\tSeek out the hermit of Zikrum-dûl\tLukíd has asked you to investigate Zikrum-dûl and seek out the mythical hermit.\n2\tSpeak with the hermit\tSpeak with the hermit at his camp in Zikrum-dûl.\n3\tReturn to Lukíd in Ub Nishir\tReturn to Lukíd in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and tell him that you found the hermit and what you saw in Zikrum-dûl.\n",
[12387]="7006F09B\n1\tComplete 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress' on any difficulty\tUse the Instance Finder to complete 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress' on any difficulty.\n2\tTalk to Mizâdi\tYou have reclaimed Dun Shûma from the Ekhamâti forces. You should talk to Mizâdi.\n",
[12388]="70066458\n1\tVisit the valley entrance\030Visit a humble warren\030Visit a comfortable warren\030Visit a hidden humble warren\030Visit a hidden comfortable warren\030Visit a grand warren\030Visit the valley market\030Visit the walls of High Sundergrót\tThe homesteads of the Holbytlan can be found south-west of the village of Lyndelby. Almetha Ditchel has bid you explore the valleys of her people and return to her once you've seen the sights of the valley.\n2\tReturn to Almetha in the valley market\tYou should return to Almetha in the valley market\n",
[12389]="70054673\n1\tDefeat morvul stalkers (total: 8)\tMorvul stalkers are hidden somewhere in the Circle of Madness. You should defeat morvul stalkers.\n2\tThe morvul stalkers have been defeated, eliminating one more threat to the Rangers of Ithilien.\t\n",
[12390]="70039FFF\n1\tDefeat Boar-tribe Orcs\tThe Boar-tribe Orcs are unpredictable and dangerous. Defeat as many of them as possible.\n2\tDefeat Boar-tribe Orcs (total: 8)\tThe Boar-tribe Orcs are unpredictable and dangerous. Defeat as many of them as possible.\n3\tCompleted\tSeveral Boar-tribe Orcs were defeated, making travel through their camp a little less dangerous.\n",
[12391]="70053049\n1\tExplore the mine entrance of Kidzul-kâlah\030Explore the lower aqueducts of Kidzul-kâlah\030Explore the upper aqueducts of Kidzul-kâlah\030Explore the water-house courtyard of Kidzul-kâlah\030Explore the water-house overlook of Kidzul-kâlah\030Explore the mountain pass in the Gladdenmere\030Explore the insides of Kidzul-kâlah's ruins\030Complete 'Shade Over Kidzul-kâlah'\030Complete 'The Chambers of Kidzul-kâlah'\tThe dwarf mine of Kidzul-kâlah can be found along the southern edge of the Gladdenmere. You should investigate the old ruins for Varthmath.\n2\tTalk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere\tVarthmath can be found at the old dock in the south-east side of the Gladdenmere. You should talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere.\n",
[12392]="70028451\n1\tTalk to Quickbeam by the Isen\tQuickbeam is at the river's edge, down in the Vale below his home. Quickbeam has asked you to meet him down by the river's edge, where he believes he has found a way to sneak you into Isengard.\n2\tSpeak with Dagoras within Isengard\tYou should sneak into Isengard through the tunnel Quickbeam has opened for you.\n",
[12393]="700608E8\n1\tMeet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap\tNáin and his company can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap. Believing that an ancient Greymaul treasury known as the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra had long laid hidden in Mount Gundabad, Prince Durin has asked you to join Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap. You should meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun.\n2\tTalk to Náin at Amgaruslun\tNáin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap. After arriving at Amgaruslun, you have found Náin's company hard at work excavating what appears to be an old passageway deeper into Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Náin.\n3\tThe Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond the frozen falls of Amgaruslun in the Clovengap. According to Prince Durin, the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond Amgaruslun in the Clovegap. You should see if the dwarves of Náin's company have broken through the ice concealing the passage to the ancient Greymaul treasury.\t\n4\tTalk to Náin at Amgaruslun\tNáin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap. The dwarves' hard work has borne fruit. You have discovered the passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should return to Náin.\n5\tComplete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'\tThe Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found in the Clovengap. Náin has asked you to muster your allies and aid Prince Durin in confronting Hrímil Frost-heart in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. NOTE: You must complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra' on any difficulty Tier to advance this quest.\n6\tTalk to Durin at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset\tPrince Durin can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset. You have triumphed over Hrímil Frost-heart at the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad.\n",
[12394]="7006028C\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\tHeirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra. You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tSwayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.\n",
[12395]="7006028E\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\tHeirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra. You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tSwayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.\n",
[12396]="7006028D\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\tHeirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra. You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tSwayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.\n",
[12397]="7006028B\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\tHeirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra. You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tSwayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.\n",
[12398]="7006028A\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\tHeirs to their fallen chieftain, Hrungrod, the ice-giants Armód, Kvethár, and Threkvegg guard the entrance to Abnankâra. You must defeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth and gain entry to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tSwayed by the power of Hrímil's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the Hobgoblins of Mount Gundabad guard the arming-chamber of Ibkêrmazal in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk and the hobgoblins under the control of Hrímil Frost-heart and gain entry to Akrazulgibshîn, the treasury of the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart slumbers in her lair within Akrazulgibshîn, the long-forgotten treasury of the Greymauls in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You must defeat Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, and put an end to her rule of Mount Gundabad.\n",
[12399]="70060E42\n1\tTalk to Drachyn\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra, tiers 1, 2, 3, and 4 instance completion deeds.\n",
[12400]="7003ED28\n1\tTalk to Vighar Roadwalker\tLarus and Vighar are at a small camp in the High Crag, east of Glóin's camp. Glóin asked you to find his friends Larus and Vighar at the High Crag camp and aid them.\n",
[12401]="700544DB\n1\tDefeat the High Sorcerer of Harad in Mordor Besieged\tThey called him the High Sorcerer of Harad, but for most of those who fought against Sauron it was just a name. He rarely left the dungeon fastnesses of Mordor, for he delighted in the working of foul rituals and the mastery of fell magics, and gave his thought to little else. But when the Dark Lord saw fit to send him forth, Men and Elves knew to give him a wide berth, or suffer. It was Mêbat he wore, the Mirth-eater, and wherever he went there was an end to laughter, and only the onset of grief.\n2\tDefeat the High Sorcerer of Harad in Mordor Besieged\tThey called him the High Sorcerer of Harad, but for most of those who fought against Sauron it was just a name. He rarely left the dungeon fastnesses of Mordor, for he delighted in the working of foul rituals and the mastery of fell magics, and gave his thought to little else. But when the Dark Lord saw fit to send him forth, Men and Elves knew to give him a wide berth, or suffer. It was Mêbat he wore, the Mirth-eater, and wherever he went there was an end to laughter, and only the onset of grief.\n3\tThe High Sorcerer of Harad, defeated but enduring\tThey called him the High Sorcerer of Harad, but for most of those who fought against Sauron it was just a name. He rarely left the dungeon fastnesses of Mordor, for he delighted in the working of foul rituals and the mastery of fell magics, and gave his thought to little else. But when the Dark Lord saw fit to send him forth, Men and Elves knew to give him a wide berth, or suffer. It was Mêbat he wore, the Mirth-eater, and wherever he went there was an end to laughter, and only the onset of grief.\n",
[12402]="7000135B\n1\tBring the orders and the money-box back to Birgir\030Collect Angmarim orders\030Collect the money-box\tAngmarim patrols can be found on the roads in Imlad Balchorth, west of Myrkworth. Birgir has asked you to waylay Angmarim patrols and recover any orders or money-boxes they may be carrying.\n",
[12403]="7003EAFB\n1\tDefeat Corcur in the South Trollshaws (total: 10)\tCorcur are encamped at the ruins of Minas Agor in the South Trollshaws. While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should deal with the Corcur encamped there.\n",
[12404]="7003EAFF\n1\tDefeat Corcur in Nan Tornaeth (total: 10)\tCorcur have begun to invade Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws. While in Nan Tornaeth, you should drive out the Corcur who have come to the Trollshaws to reclaim their lands of old.\n",
[12405]="7006BB60\n1\tReach Khûn Sagaz\tEnârshan has asked you to travel to Khûn Sagaz at the top of the hill nearby to investigate.\n2\tLocate where supplies are kept in Khûn Sagaz\030Locate where weapons are kept in Khûn Sagaz\030Defeat Orcs in Khûn Sagaz (total: 5)\tInvestigate Khûn Sagaz near the Falls of Ilûritu for Enârshan the Idâmi.\n3\tReturn to Enârshan behind the waterfall in Ilûritu\tReturn to Enârshan in her home behind the waterfall in Ilûritu.\n",
[12406]="7002669F\n1\tHelp Maladan scout Arthobel\030Aid Nethrandir with the robbers of Tham Sarch\030Aid Nethrandir with the mirrors of Tham Sarch\030Aid Rodlam with the robbers of Tham Laegamon\030Aid Rodlam with the longbows of Tham Laegamon\tThe crypts line the Way of Kings leading into Annúminas. Before the Rangers can move to investigate the state of the crypts within the Way of Kings, they must secure the hills from the remaining tomb-robbers. Nimbellas has asked you to do this.\n2\tTalk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings\tNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp along the Way of Kings. The hills have been cleared of threats. You should return at once to Nimbellas.\n",
[12407]="7000EAAF\n1\tCollect the reins from Matti\030Collect the salt lick from Kaleva\030Collect the saddle from Rauno\tIlmo has asked you to collect a saddle from Rauno, reins from Matti, and a salt lick from Kaleva within Sûri-kylä.\n2\tTalk to Ilmo\030Collect Elk-saddle\030Collect Elk-reins\030Collect Salt-lick\tIlmo is outside of Sûri-kylä with his elk-herd. You should bring the items you collected to Ilmo at once.\n",
[12408]="70037837\n1\tTalk to Éothain\tArcil suggested that you explore the former capital city of Rohan, Aldburg and learn something of its history. You should seek out Éothain and speak with him first.\n2\tExplore the Aldburg training hall\tThe training hall is in the eastern part of Aldburg. Éothain recommended starting your exploration of Aldburg at the training hall.\n3\tTalk to Téothic\tTéothic is at the training hall in Aldburg. You should speak with Téothic about the Aldburg training hall.\n4\tExplore the Aldburg stable\tThe stable of Aldburg is to the north-west of the training hall. Téothic recommended that you go see the stable next.\n5\tTalk to Wilflad\tWilflad is near the stable of Aldburg. Wilflad may be able to provide more information about the stable.\n6\tExplore the Quartermaster's house\tThe Quartermaster's house is located in the western portion of Aldburg. Wilflad suggested that you visit the Quartermaster of Aldburg.\n7\tTalk to Bertred\tBertred is at his house in the western part of Aldburg. Wilflad told you to speak with Bertred, Quartermaster of Aldburg, to learn more of the city's history.\n8\tTalk to Arcil\tArcil is at the Mead Hall of Aldburg. You have explored Aldburg and learned a little about its history. You should now return to Arcil.\n",
[12409]="70057182\n1\tTravel to Avabárg\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should travel to Avabárg.\n2\tTalk to Léothred at Avabárg\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n3\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n4\tTalk to Léothred elsewhere in Avabárg\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n5\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n6\tDefeat Orcs at Avabárg (total: 6)\tOrcs can be found at Avabárg. You should defeat Orcs at Avabárg.\n7\tTalk to Léothred elsewhere in Avabárg\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n8\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n9\tTalk to Léothred elsewhere in Avabárg\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n10\tContinue learning the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n11\tTalk to Léothred at Avabárg\tAvabárg can be found in Woodsedge in the Vales of Anduin. You should talk to Léothred at Avabárg.\n",
[12410]="700156F8\n1\tThe grodbog-lair is in the Palace of Náin, north of Lamâb-dûm. Thórhall asked you to take the scent-glands to the grodbog-hive and crush them. The resulting scent should draw forth the hive-queen.\t\n2\tTalk to Thórhall at Lamab-dûm\tThórhall is at the small dwarf-camp in Lamab-dûm, south of the Palace of Náin. You should report back to Thórhall with news of your success.\n",
[12411]="70062F41\n1\tBring the hobby horse to Cai\tMellanion has asked you to bring his hobby horse to Cai. Cai is in the inn, in Herne.\n",
[12412]="700268CD\n1\tSave Umín from the necklace's hold\t\n",
[12413]="7004A8E5\n1\tDefeat and burn Zhavár-hai in Dath Nethryn (total: 8)\tZhavár-hai can be found in the shallows of Dath Nethryn in southern Lhingris. Legolas has spotted numerous Zhavár-hai roaming the foetid swamp of Dath Nethryn in Lhingris. Even if the Orcs are slain, the insects and spiders within them pose a great threat, so he has advised you to burn them after defeating them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated and burned many of the Zhavár-hai in Dath Nethryn.\n",
[12414]="7004ABA1\n1\tComplete Kála-murg: The Hordes of Ungol\tCandúr can be found in Udûn. You should talk Candúr.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted Kála-murg: The Hordes of Ungol.\n",
[12415]="700377A4\n1\tProtect the Hornburg\tThe Hornburg is the final layer of Rohan's defences at Helm's Deep. If it falls, then all hope is lost.\n",
[12416]="70037DD9\n1\tProtect the dike\t\n",
